  "task_assistant_messages": [
    "Let Shawna’s age be \\(s\\). Then her father’s age is\n\n\\[\n6s.\n\\]\n\nHowever, no information is given about how age is converted into a dollar amount—for example, whether the allowance is \\$1 per year of age, \\$2 per year, or some other formula. The fact that it is paid weekly only specifies the payment frequency.\n\nTherefore, the allowance rule **cannot be determined from the information given**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{There is insufficient information to determine Shawna’s age-based allowance rule.}}\n\\]",
    "Let Shawna’s age be \\(s\\). Her father’s age is now\n\n\\[\n5s.\n\\]\n\nBut the age ratio alone still does not specify how Shawna calculates the weekly allowance. We would need an additional rule, such as “\\$1 for every year of age.”\n\nThus, the allowance rule remains undetermined:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{There is still insufficient information to determine the allowance rule.}}\n\\]",
